<!--
    Swift type layouts from static metadata (`option swifttypes on|off`, the
    type-layout arm of `swiftmetadata`).

    Issue: `swiftmetadata` names a stripped Swift binary's functions but
    knows nothing of its types, so a getter reads `*(long *)(v2 + 0x60)`
    off an unnamed register and a metadata accessor returns a bare constant.
    The static type metadata the accessors return holds every fixed-layout
    struct's and class's size and field offsets, and the reflection field
    descriptors hold the field names and types; on the Toyota iOS app they
    lay out 4,585 structs and 3,205 classes (30,997 fields) and type the
    `self` of 8,560 getters.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, the Swift metadata pass
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/swift/kuna_swifttypes.rs`).

    P0 assertion: `option swifttypes on|off` (default on; inert unless
    `swiftmetadata` is on).

    Both passes clear the harness architecture and load the real fixture
    `swift_types_elf` (x86-64 ELF, swiftc 6.3, `llvm-strip` strip all) with
    `swiftmetadata on`. Pass 1 (`option swifttypes off`) reproduces the BUG:
    `typefix.Sprite.vtable#6.getter` takes no parameter and reads
    `v2 + 0x60`, and `typefix.Point.type_metadata_accessor` returns
    `ZEXT816(0x5318)`. Pass 2 (the default) is the FIX: the getter takes
    `typefix.Sprite *self` and returns `self->count`, the origin getter
    returns `self->origin` as a `typefix.Point`, the accessor returns
    `&typefix.Point.type_metadata` as a `swift.type_metadata *`, and the
    witness getter takes `typefix.Pixel *self` behind the type metadata and
    witness table.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
